{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-175575",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The truth set of $P(x)∨Q(x)$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∨Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{1,3,9\\}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=∅,\n$$\n\n \nthe empty set, since there are no positive integers $x$ less than $1.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∨Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,9\\}\\cup ∅ \\\\  & =\\{1,3,9\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
